{
    int sum = x + y;
    <code>Debug.Assert(sum >= x && sum >= y);</code>
    return sum;
}
```

The script works by first compiling a regular expression that recognizes "@@@" and every word after it, separated by spaces.
It then finds all matches in the code and replaces them with an HTML <code></code> block that represents the Assert statement. It assumes that the Assert condition is in the form of a comment following the "@@@" pattern, for example, "/// @@@ sum is greater than or equal to x and y".


